<title>SWEDEN: Foreningsbanken 9-mo profit rises 7 pct.</title>
<headline>Foreningsbanken 9-mo profit rises 7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish commercial bank Foreningsbanken reports for nine months to September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit			   811  vs     758</p>
<p> Credit losses				750  vs   1,084</p>
<p> Profit before credit losses	  1,561  vs   1,842</p>
<p> Interest receivable		    8,307  vs  8,707</p>
<p> Leasing income				67  vs     72</p>
<p> Interest payable			 5,712  vs  5,911</p>
<p> Dividends received			  10  vs	6</p>
<p> Commissions receiveable		  603  vs    530</p>
<p> Commissions payable			 36  vs     42</p>
<p> Net profit on financial ops	    132  vs    247</p>
<p> Other operating income		   369  vs    391</p>
<p> Total income			     3,740  vs  4,000</p>
<p> Admin, staff costs		     1,880  vs  1,859</p>
<p> Depreciation				 125  vs    141</p>
<p> Other operating costs		    174  vs    158</p>
<p> Total costs				2,179  vs  2,158</p>
<p> Net profit				   762  vs    758</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full company name Foreningsbanken AB.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
